-      "edescr": "0:Cruise ON, 1:Cruise Ready, 2:Decel, 3:CarrotCruise, 4:Following gap. Mode 4: right decreases to 1, left increases to 4; one step per press, no hold repeat. Requires openpilot longitudinal control and four gap levels. Entering/leaving mode 4 requires a restart; gap changes while in mode 4 apply while driving. Existing paddle output interlocks remain.",
+      "edescr": "0:Cruise ON, 1:Cruise Ready, 2:Decel, 3:CarrotCruise, 4:Following gap. Mode 4: only during normal cruise ON, right decreases to 1 and left increases to 4. Regen input during standby, OFF, CANCEL or independent SoftHold preserves the saved gap on re-engagement. A paddle held from OFF must be released and newly pressed after ON. An accepted ON request may finish saving after OFF; direct gap button/web changes remain allowed while OFF; one step per press, no hold repeat. Requires openpilot longitudinal control and four gap levels. Entering/leaving mode 4 requires a restart; gap changes while in mode 4 apply while driving. On MQ4 HEV CANFD camera-SCC with openpilot longitudinal control, a new mode-4 gesture in normal ACC keeps the ACC request continuous. CANCEL, pedals and independent SoftHold interlocks remain; regen-state preservation needs vehicle validation.",
